		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=28503#p28503"><![CDATA[
Hello everybody,<br>Here is a brief overview of what I made at Golaem with the Bullet Physics SDK:<br><img src="http://www.golaem.com/sites/default/files/images/screenshots/PhysicsEngine.jpg" class="postimage" alt="Image"><br><br>A video showing it in action can be seen here: <a href="http://youtu.be/fKo-AsAvySk" class="postlink">http://youtu.be/fKo-AsAvySk</a><br><br>In short, the soft is a crowd simulation software embedded within Maya, and the ragdoll part of our character was made thanks to Bullet Physics.<br><br>Thanks Erwinn for this beautiful tool <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_wink.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=";)" title="Wink"> Next on the wish list would be multithread support for windows 64 bits platforms :p<br><br>You can see more about the software here: <a href="http://youtu.be/5YhPOntJtx0" class="postlink">http://youtu.be/5YhPOntJtx0</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8790">Yann</a> — Thu Aug 09, 2012 3:34 pm</p><hr />
